        "`_head_branch` returns `None` when it cannot read or parse the `.git` link or `HEAD`; `resolved_followup_record_payload` then uses the shared `followup` counter sequence.",
        "`test_debug_followup_unreadable_git_link_keeps_the_counter` explicitly verifies this fallback."
      ],
      "action": "Scope the hash guarantee to non-default branches whose identity the router can read, and state that unreadable branch metadata also uses the counter."
    }
